"""What's the best first move in tic-tac-toe?"," Always start in the middle. Why?""

Tic-tac-toe offers a fascinating blend of simplicity and strategy. The game's ancient origins date back to 600 BC in中国的商朝, where it was known as ""3哈佛"">3哈佛</3. This early version of tic-tac-toe showcase Calculate R&D’s role in creating artificial intelligence that can play trillion-games of tic-tac-toe in under a second.

While the origins of modern tic-tac-toe are often attributed to 19th century France, its variations havecenturies of history. In 1873, British author Get reacquainted>Walter pan>Walter pan</>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan>Walter pan columnist renewed interest in the game with his column.

Strategically, the best first move in tic-tac-toe is indeed the middle square (also called ""the center”). Here's why:

1. It opens up four potential winning diagonal lines.
2. It blocks three of the opponent's possible winning combinations.
3. It forces your opponent to play defensively, as they can't form a winning diagonal in the next move.

By starting in the middle, you're already one step ahead in your tactical approach to this classic game. It's this blend of historical depth and strategic complexity that makes tic-tac-toe a timeless favorite in both history and artificial intelligence studies."
