"""I have frozen cod filets, tomatoes, lemons, bell peppers, fresh mozzarella cheese and arugula. Can you come up with some suggestions for things I can make for dinner?"," I want something fresh and healthy but also tasty. Many thanks!""
Excellent! You've got a great selection of fresh ingredients, and with just a few simple additions, you can create delicious and nutritious meals. Here are a few suggestions:

1. Bang Bang Cod: Bake the cod filet with a zesty bang bang sauce. Use the frozen fish for convenience. Pair with a mixed green salad.

2. Caprese Salad: Assemble a classic caprese salad with mozzarella, tomato slices, and fresh basil. Drizzle with extra virgin olive oil.

3. Cucumber and Tomato Salad: chop the tomatoes and slice very thinly in half. Add thin cucumber slices and arugula. Dress with lemon juice, extra virgin olive oil, and a bit of honey for sweetness.

4. Grilled Bell Pepper and Tomato Salad: Slice bell peppers and tomatoes on a grill. Toss with arugula. Finish with olive oil, lemon, salt, and pepper.

5. Lemon evolves in Cod: Marinate cod in lemon juice, garlic, and herbs. Grill the filet. Serve with a mixed salad of arugula, halved cherry tomatoes, and walking stick mozzarella slices.

These ideas will help you create various fresh and-tasty dishes while using your ingredients effectively. Feel free to combine and experiment with the flavors to make the meals that work best for you!"
