"""How to analyze PostgreSQL memory usage?"," Memory management for high-performance PostgreSQL databases.

PostgreSQL uses memory for various purposes including:
- Buffering query results
- Tracking open transactions
- Storing index and operator routines
- Maintaining session state and connection pools
- deadline-driven scheduling algorithms

Strategies to optimize PostgreSQL memory usage:
- Use paginators instead of requesting large result sets
- Adjust the shared memory size according to database size and query workload
- Limit the number of parallel queries using the append huge pages option to reduce fragmentiation
- Minimize the size of data types and columns to use less memory
- Use password hashing to ensure secure memory usage duringAuthentication
- Regularly analyze and tune page backing eternal buffers and shared memory objects
- Utilize vacuumBackgroundWithBackgroundw option to free up Utility memory

By effectively managing memory in PostgreSQL, administrators can enhance query performance and maintain a balance between application performance and memory usage.
"""
