"""How to create a database model with sqlalchemy?"," This example shows how to create a SQLAlchemy model for a simple library system. The model includes classes for Book, Author, and Book copy.""

In this example, we are going to create a database model using SQLAlchemy for a simple library system. We'll define three classes: Book, Author, and BookCopy. 

1. The Book class will have an ID, title, and author ID.
2. The Author class will have an ID and name.
3. The BookCopy class will have an ID, book ID, and status.

Here's the SQLAlchemy model for the simple library system:

```python
from sqlalchemy import create_engine
from sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker
from models import Base, Book, Author, BookCopy

engine = create_engine('sqlite:///library.db')
Base.metadata.create_all(engine)

Session = sessionmaker(bind=engine)
session = Session()

# Add some sample data
book1 = Book(title=""The Catcher in the Rye"", author_id=""1"")
author1 = Author(name=""J.D. Salinger"")
-session.add(book1)
