4 rounds of:
- 10 minute jump rope
- 5 rounds of 50 push-ups
- 5 rounds of 50 sit-ups
- 10 minutes of light jogging

 Thursday:
 Warm up with 5 minutes of light running or jumping jacks
4 rounds of:
- 10 minutes on the treadmill at 9 mph
- 50 square push-ups
- 50 square sit-ups
- 10 minutes on the bike at moderate intensity

 Saturday:
 Warm up with 5 minutes of light running or jumping jacks
4 rounds of:
- 10 minutes of layering exercises (Heywood, 1995)
- 50 squats
- 50 bicep curls
- 10 minutes of swimming

This plan combines intense cardiovascular exercise (jump roping, running, swimming, and layering) with strength training (push-ups, sit-ups, squats, and bicep curls). It's designed to burns calories, build muscle, and improve overall fitness. Remember to consult with a fitness professional before starting any new exercise routine."
