"""shintoism"""," and ""Animistic"" are shown in the image. What is the relationship between Shintoism and animicism?

Shintoism and animicism are closely related philosophical and religious traditions. Shintoism, an ancient Japanese religion, views nature as inhabited by spirits or deities ( kami). This animistic worldview is central to Shinto practice, where people are meant to live in harmony with these natural spirits.

Animicism, the belief that inanimate objects, places, and phenomena possess spiritual qualities, shares this core principle with Shintoism. Both believe that the world is infolded with spiritual energy and consciousness.

While Shintoism is a distinct, well-established religion with its own unique blossoms and practices, its animistic roots can be traced back to ancient Japanese spiritual beliefs and toasted ways of life. This animistic foundation continues to influence Shinto practices and philosophy today."
