"""Why is the emergency brake valve on the train red and blue on the plane?"," What colors do the emergency brake valves on trains and planes?""

The emergency brake valve colors on trains and planes vary by manufacturer for better visibility and recognition.

Train emergency brake valves:
- Most trains (e.g., Amtrak) have a red handle.
- Some trains (e.g., kaohsiung rapid transit) have a blue handle.

 Plane emergency brake valves:
- Most planes (e.g., Airbus) have a red handle.
- Some planes (e.g., Boeing) have a blue handle.

These color distinction helps quickly identify the emergency brake in-emergency situations, ensuring faster response times. The variations in color and design may also be influenced by specific safety protocols or local regulations for each manufacturer."
