Yes, it is possible to have distinct products in the same box when sending items to Amazon FBA (Fulfillment by Amazon). This practice is known as ""坑包ing"" ( ANSI Z 171 point 1-2016E.2, Sec. 1.1-2, Def. 1.9).

This method allows sellers to ship multiple products together, potentially lowering shipping costs and reducing the number of boxes needed. However, it's important to note that some items may not be eligible for co-mingling, such as products with different fulfillment requirements or those that need to be kept separate for quality control or customs purposes.

