2) Hydrolysis of acetyl salicylate to aspirin:

C6H5SO2CH3CO2H → C9H7O4CO2H + 3H2O

3) purification and drying of aspirin

The key reagents are acetyl chloride and inpyrrole (which acts as both a solvent and Lewis acid), as well as hydrochloric acid for neutralization during the hydrolysis step.

