"""can you write quick sort in python"""," Yes, here's a quick sort implementation in Python:

def quick_sort(arr):
    if len(arr) < 2:
        return arr
    pivot = arr[len(arr)//2]  # Selecting the middle element as pivot
    left = [x for x in arr if x < pivot]  # Elements less than pivot
    right = [x for x in arr if x > pivot]  # Elements greater than pivot
    return quick_sort(left) + [pivot] + quick_sort(right)

This function sorts an array using the quick sort algorithm. It recursively partitions the array into smaller subarrays and then combines them back to form a sorted list."
