"""Do midi keyboards usually accept midi clock messages or otherwise allow for setting the tempo externally?","If yes, how would I go about doing this? Also, if not, what's the best way to alternatively synchronized tempo with existingmidi files?""

MIDI keyboards typically do accept MIDI clock messages, which allow for external tempo synchronization. To set the tempo externally:

1. Look for a ""MIDI Clock"" or ""Clock In"" button on your keyboard or all-in-one music production system.

2. Connect your MIDI clock device to the appropriate port on your MIDI keyboard or computer.

3. Press the corresponding clock button, and your MIDI keyboard should start synchronizing its tempo with the external clock.

Alternatively, many MIDI keyboards and DAWs (Digital Audio Workstations) offer software-based tempo settings:

1. In your DAW, open your MIDI track.

2. Use the tempo slider to manually adjust your desired tempo.

3. For precise tuning, you might need to use the fine-tune or temperedhands function.

