To build a brighter day, we can.

This progress, this history before us,
300 years of tightly bunched buses,
A progress each new era traveler,
The globe's expanding, cloaked in velvet.

So from the old to the new we see,
A silent farther we travel,
Share all the thoughts, Share all the news,
In this big world yet newly dusk."
