"""How can a poor person make a million dollars in only a few months?"," Well, the short answer is, they can't,"" said Mike Johnson,Owner/Realtor of Mike Johnson Real Estate Team.
Mike, a third-generation real estate professional in Stone Mountain, emphasized that the idea of rapid wealth accumulation for those in poverty is a myth. He explained that the path to significant financial success in real estate, like any venture, requires hard work, time, and usually some initial capital.
 âWhen I started in this business 15 years ago, I had no money,"" Mike recalled. ""I had to borrow from my parents to get my first car and buy my first house to sell. But I'm still here afterall. It took time, but it was possible.â
 Johnson stressed that real estate has a learning curve, and it's crucial for newcomers to be realistic about their starting point and the time it might take to see significant returns on their investments."
