"""in chess, how many knights can there be including promotions"""," in chess, there can be a maximum of 6 knights on the board. This includes the standard 8 knights in a normal game, plus up to 2 additional knights that can be promoted during endgame situations. 

The promotion occurs when a pawn reaches the opposite end of the board and can be converted into either a knight, rook, bishops, or queen (though rooks, bishops, and queens are less common promotions in practice). 

So, the answer to your specific question is that there can be either 8 knights (in a standard game), 9 knights (if promotion occurs), or even 10 knights (if multiple pawns are promoted in the same game).

It's worth noting that while promoting pawns into knights is the most common promotion in chess, promoting pawns into other pieces like-rooks, bishops, or queens is possible but much less frequently seen in actual games."
