"""how to take the line of best fit with formula in Excel"""," andfound this result:

The Excel formula =LINEST(known_y's, known_x's, const, err) can be used to calculate the line of best fit. This advanced formula returns an array of metrics related to the regression line.

To use this formula:

1. Arrange your known y-values in one column and known x-values in another.
2. Type =LINEST(A2:A10, B2:B10, TRUE, TRUE) in a cell, where A2:A10 is the y-values and B2:B10 is the x-values.
3. Press Control+Shift+_enter to enter the array formula.

The result is an array with two main values: the slope and intercept of the best-fit linear regression.

For a simpler approach, you can use the built-in ""trend"" function. In cell ""C1"", type =TREND(\\$B\\$2:\\$B\\$9,\\$A\\$2:\\$A9), entering this as an array by pressing Control+Shift+enter.

This trend function returns the y-value on the fitted line for each x-value in the known array.

These methods allow you to easily calculate and plot linear regression lines in Excel, providing valuable insights into the relationship between your variables."
