"""provide instructions and code snippets  to allow downloading wallpaper for cell phones from a webpage"""," Here's a step-by-step guide with code snippets to download wallpapers for cell phones from a webpage:

1. First, you'll need to identify the wallpaper images on the website. Let's assume they're displayed in a <ul> element:

```html
<ul>
  <li>Wallpaper 1</li>
  <li>Wallpaper 2</li>
  <li>Wallpaper 3</li>
</ul>
```

2. You'll need to write a script to loop through each wallpaper image and download it. We'll use jQuery for this:

```javascript
$( document ).ready( function(){
  $('ul').each( function(){
    var $li = $( this );
    $li.find( 'img' ).each(function(){
      var $img = $( this );
      var src = $img.attr( 'src' );

      // Check if the image is available before downloading
      if( src != '' ){
        $.ajax({
          url: src,
          type: 'GET',
          dataType: 'image',
          success function( response ){
            // response is now the image data
            // You can save the image here
            

            // Stream the image using base64 encoded data
            var reader = new FileReader();
            reader.onload = function( event ){
              var blob = new Blob( [ event.target.result ] );
              var url = URL.createObjectURL( blob );

              var link = document.createElement( 'a' );
              link.href = url;
              link.download = 'wallpaper-' + $li.index() + '.png';
              document.body.appendChild(link);
            }
          }
        });
      }
    });
  });
});
```

3. This script loops through each <li>, finds the <img>, checks if there's a source, and then downloads the image using AJAX. It streams the image using base64 data and allows the user to click a link to save it to their device.

This will give users the option to download wallpapers directly from the webpage. Keep in mind that if you're serving this from your own website, you'll need to ensure you have the necessary rights to distribute the images."
