"""Grevillea Poorinda Royal Mantle"""," is the result of careful breeding that aimed to improve upon the classic ""Grevillea poorinda"". This cultivar maintains a compact, mounded form, but adds deep, velvety burgundy foliage that provides a stunning contrast to its Original Poorinda leaves.

The leaves of ""Grevillea Poorinda Royal Mantle"" are slightly smaller than the Original Poorinda, creating a more dense, carpet-like appearance. They still retain the characteristic silvery sheen and Sansevieria-like texture, but are far more intense in color.

The mining faculty of the Grevillea species is well represented in this plant, with new growth typically initiated between 5-15 cm above the previous year's growth point. This characteristic mining pattern helps the plant adjust to environmental stressors and offers Hands-On resilience in dry conditions.

Grevillea poorinda Royal Mantle is an excellent choice for rock gardens, borders, or containers due to its compact size (reaching heights of about 3-6 feet) and striking appearance. It thrives in full-sun to part-shade environments and prefers well-draining soil.

This plant is resistance to salt spray and is relatively drought-tolerant, making it well-suited for coastal or arid environments. Its hardiness allows it to withstand rainy periods and occasional frosts, with minimal maintenance required."
