"""how can i generate checked exceptions in java inside lambda functions?"," also any links regarding lambda expressions in java? with regards, """"""

To generate checked exceptions in Java inside lambda functions, you can use the throwing keyword. Here's an example:

```java
double divide(double a, double b) {
    return a / b;
}

int main() {
    double result = divide(10, 0)
        .orElseThrow(() -> new ArithmeticException(""circular reference""));
}
```

To learn more about lambda expressions in Java, you can refer to the official Java documentation:

<https://docs.oracle.com/en/javaächtliche-sprache/pdf/java8.pdf>

Additionally, there are many tutorials and videos available on various platforms like YouTube, Pluralsight, and Coursera that explain lambda expressions in detail."
