"""Write some C code for me that creates an array, and then resizes this array to fit one more element."""," Certainly! Here's a C code snippet that demonstrates creating an array and then resizing it to fit an additional element:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    int myArray[4];
    printf(""Original array size: %d elements\\n"", sizeof(myArray) / sizeof(int));
    
    // Resize the array to fit 5 elements
    int *newArray = realloc(myArray, 5 * sizeof(int));
    if (newArray) {
        printf(""Resized array size: %d elements\\n"", sizeof(newArray) / sizeof(int));
    } else {
        printf(""Array resizing failed\\n"");
        return 1;
    }
}
```

This code first initializes a small array of 4 integers. Then, it uses the `realloc` function to resize the array to accommodate 5 elements. The realloc function returns a pointer to the new, larger memory块, which is then assigned to the `newArray` pointer. If the resizing is successful, the program prints the new size of the array. If it fails, an error message is displayed."
