"""A 2g disc of copper is dropped into a 12g glass of water. If the copper was at 85\\u00b0C and the water was at 70\\u00b0C, what is the new temperature of the mixture?","}\\宣告
{""What is the new temperature of the mixture?""}


{The new temperature of the mixture is 75.5\\u00b0C. This can be determined using the principle of heat exchange, where the temperatures of the hotter and colder substances Adjust to reach equilibrium. The copper, being warmer than the water, will release heat, while the water, being cooler, will absorb heat. This process will continue until both substances reach the same temperature, which is the equilibrium temperature of the mixture.}"
