"""what is the different between a rabbit and an elephant"""," The main differences between a rabbit and an elephant are:

Rabbits have small legs and large ears, while elephants have large ears but very large tusks and a large body.

Rabbits can hop over long distances due to their powerful legs, while elephants use tools with their trunks for everyday tasks.

Rabbits typically have multiple ears, described as ""two little ears,"" whereas elephants have a single large ear.

