"""How can I install the numpy pacakage from the github repo on a linux machine?","?"" This question is written on using colored text

To install numpy from the GitHub repo on a Linux machine, you'll need to:

1. Clone the repository:
   ```
   git clone https://github.comnumpy/numpy.git
   ```

2. Navigate into the cloned directory:
   ```
   cd numpy
   ```

3. Install dependencies:
   ```
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

4. Install numpy:
   ```
   python setup.py install
   ```

5. Verify the installation:
   ```
   python -c ""import numpy; print(numpy.__version__)""
   ```

This process assumes you have Python and pip installed on your system. You might need to set up your Python environment or virtual environment to work with thegit repo."
