"""make me laugh"""," is written on a sheet of paper. The writing takes up 80% of the available space on the sheet. If the sheet is 12 inches by 9 inches, how many square inches of the sheet are not written on?

To solve this problem, we need to:
1. Calculate the total area of the sheet
2. Calculate the area occupied by the writing
3. Subtract the writing area from the total area

Step 1: Calculate the total area of the sheet
Total area = Length × Width
Total area = 12 inches × 9 inches = 108 square inches

Step 2: Calculate the area occupied by the writing
Writing area = 80% of total area
Writing area = 0.80 × 108 square inches = 86.4 square inches

Step 3: Calculate the area not written on
Area not written = Total area - Writing area
Area not written = 108 square inches - 86.4 square inches = 21.6 square inches

Therefore, 21.6 square inches of the sheet are not written on."
