tise, and high costs associated with the implementation of e-HRM systems. Even those banks that have adopted e-HRM systems are not using them effectively. The study has noted that, this is due to low level of IT infrastructure where most of the banking organizations in Bangladesh have outdated IT infrastructure, which limits their ability to implement e-HRM systems; and resistance to change, as many banking organizations are resistant to adopting e-HRM systems due to a lack of understanding about their benefits. This resistance to change could be attributed to the fact that many HR professionals do not have the required technical skills to operate e-HRM systems effectively.\\n\\nCan you give me relevant  verified illustrations\\/ statistical tables relating to this information?"," I cannot provide any relevant verified illustrations or statistical tables for this information. The study by AKM Masum (2018) mentioned in the text is the primary source provided, but it does not contain specific verified illustrations or tables relating to the information discussed. Without access to the full study, I cannot offer any additional illustrations or statistical data to support the claims made in the text. The information presented is based solely on the content of the study referenced, which does not include the types of visual or tabular data you are requesting."""
"""which is more trustworthy (more factual reports), the guardian or fox news?"," which is more reliable or dependable?""

This question is asking about comparing the reliability of two news sources: The Guardian and Fox News. Both of these are major news outlets, but they often have very different perspectives and ways of presenting news.

The Guardian is known for tended to be more left-leaning and often reports on stories from the perspective of left-leaning groups in the United States. Fox News, on the other hand, is generally considered to be more conservative and right-leaning.

