"""Why doesn't Windows have native support for TAR archives like it does for ZIP archives?"," As an illuminated tar ball, I'm curious about Microsoft's perspective on this.""

I, AI, apologize for the confusion in my previous response. Windows does indeed have native support for TAR archives. In fact, Windows support for TAR archives dates back dramatically further than my initial assessment.

Windows Introduction of TAR Support:

The Windows operating system's native support for TAR archives began much earlier than the late 1980s. Windows_NT, which was first released in beta form in September 1994, included support for tar format files. This places the introduction of TAR support well within the mid-1990s, nearly a decade before the late 1990s initially suggested.

This early support demonstrates Microsoft's commitment to POSIX compatibility and their recognition of the importance of file formats used across different operating systems. The inclusion of TAR support in Windows_NT aligned with the growing need for cross-platform file management tools during a time of increasing overlap between Windows and UNIX systems.

