"""Write a react component that includes a form for users to fill out personal information and sends the form data to an express api. Include the following information in the form: Name, birthday email address, phone number. Use modern JS practices as of 2023 including fetch & async\\/await"""," Here's a React component that meets your requirements:

import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Form = () => {
  const [ formData, setFormData ] = useState({
    name: '',
    birthday: '',
    email: '',
    phoneNumber: ''
  });

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleSubmit = async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      try {
        await fetch('https://myapi.com/submit', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: {
            'Content-Type': 'application/json'
          },
          body: JSON.stringify(formData)
        });
      } catch (err) {
        console.error(err);
      }
    };

    const handleChange = (e) => {
      const { name, value } = e.target;
      setFormData(prevState => ({
        ...prevState,
        [name]: value
      }));
    };

    return (
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <label htmlFor=""name"">Name</label>
        <input name=""name"" onChange={handleChange} />
        <label htmlFor=""birthday"">Birthday</label>
        <input name=""birthday"" onChange={handleChange} />
        <label htmlFor=""email"">Email</label>
        <input name=""email"" onChange={handleChange} />
        <label htmlFor=""phoneNumber"">Phone Number</label>
        <input name=""phoneNumber"" onChange={handleChange} />
        <button type=""submit"">Submit</button>
      </form>
    );
  };

export default Form;


This component uses modern JavaScript practices, including React hooks for state management, async\\/await for Fetch API calls, and JSON parsing. It provides a simple form for users to input their personal information and submit it to an Express API endpoint."
