"""What is a thrembometer?"," What does it do?""

A thermometer is a device used to measure body temperature. It helps determine if someone has a fever or if their temperature is within a normal range.

Thermometers can be used in different ways:
1. Oral: Placed under the tongue
2. Rectal: Placed in the rectum
3. Armpit: Placed in the armpit
4. Forehead: Used with special devices or forehead thermometers
5. Under the nose: Using a special nasal strip

The reading on a thermometer typically shows temperature in degrees, usually Celsius (C) or Fahrenheit (°F). For most people, normal body temperature is around 37°C (98.6°F).

Different types of thermometers may give slightly different readings, but they all serve the same important purpose of monitoring body temperature for health reasons."
