"". Yes, you're quite right. I made a mistake in calculating the volume. For a cube with 4 units on each side, the volume would indeed be 64 cubic units, whereas the tetrahedron would have a volume of approximately 34.64 cubic units. This means the cube does in fact have a larger volume for the same wall area.

Thank you for catching that error.""

