"""Explain why when documents are signed at the top, the person filling the document is more likely to be honnest than when he sign at the bottom ?","""
The placement of a signature on a document can influence the likelihood of honest behavior in various ways.

Firstly, signing at the top of a document creates a visual barrier between the signsatory and the content they're agreeing to. This separation might create a psychological distance, potentially leading to less careful consideration of the document's contents.

In contrast, signing at the bottom involves the signatory reviewing the entire document before placing their signature at the bottom. This process forces the signatory to engage with the full contents of the document, promoting a more thorough understanding of what they're agreeing to.

Secondly, topSIGNING can imply a sense of finality or commitment. People might be morelikely to lengthy contemplation before committing their name in this position.
 
BottomSigning involves a more methodical approach, where individuals are encourages to visually examine and comparethe document's contents and their signature place before finalizing their agreement.

By promoting more thoughtful engagement with the document's content and requiring a visual comparison between signing and content, bottom-signing encourages a higher level of honesty and responsibility from the signatory.

This aligns with best practices in document design andagreement creation, asiception boyfriendpoints out. However, it's important to note that while bottom-signing can promote honesty, other structural and process elements of anagreement also play crucial roles in ensuring both parties'合法权益 are protected."
