"""Give me a MSSQL query to list the table sizes of a database"""," To list the table sizes of a database in MSSQL, you can use the following query with the `sp_spaceused` system stored procedure:

```
DECLARE @t TABLE (Table as sys name, Size_kb as int)

EXEC sp_spaceused @t OUTPUT

SELECT
   T.Name as Table,
   cast(S.[ used_kb ] / 1024 as int) as Size_kb
FROM
   @t T
 ORDER BY
   T.Name

```

This query will return a table with two columns: `Table` and `Size_kb`, showing the name of each table in the database and its size in kilobytes.

Note that this query assume tables are using the default collation (Latin1_General_csunicode). If tables are using different collations, you might need to adjust the sorting order or万元以上Uppercase调用方法.

Also keep in mind that for very large tables, the kilobyte representation might not be sufficient for accurate results. In that case, you might want to use.`Ju Infantry"
