"""How can I run a LLM local, on my laptop?","?"" - samfree

To run a Local LLM on your laptop, follow these steps:

1. install Python
2. get the openai-python library: `pip install openai`
3. fork the fine-tune ❤️ repo
4. clone your forked repo: `git clone https://github.com/<your_username>/fine-tune.git`
5. navigate to the repo: `cd fine-tune`
6. set environment vars: `export API_KEY="" your openai key `"" and `export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=""all""`
7. run the script: `python run.py`

This setup allows you to fine-tune Large Language Models (LLMs) locally, giving you control over your data and: 

- Potential cost savings
- Data security, as your data isn't sent to cloud services for training
- The ability to fine-tune: GPT, BERT, T5, RoBERTa models

Remember to replace your 'openai key' with an actual key. If you need help, feel free to ask for more clarification. happy coding!"
