"""when i played chess online i later checked the replay and on one move there were icons saying !! what is that?"," is it some kind of warning?""

The icons you're seeing during your chess game online are likely alertness indicators or time warnings. These symbols appear when a player is in a dangerous position or approaching a critical moment in the game.

Alertness icons might indicate that a player is in a risky endgame situation where they may be close to mate but also potentially in danger of losing. These icons serve as a visual prompt for players to breaking point or McCar-Apron mate them.

Time warning icons typically appear when a player is running low on time. These might consist of a stopwatch or countdown timer, reminding players that they're getting close to the time limit. In chaotic online games, these icons can sometimes be missed, causing players to exceed the time limit without realizing.

It's important to note that these icons are designed to help players, not to Prevent them from playing their strongest moves. They're there to guide players through key moments in the game and alert them when they're in a vulnerable position!

These visual cues are especially valuable in online chess where players might be juggling multiple games simultaneously or dealing with other distractions that could affect their focus and play."
