"""Write an article about proper use of cloud based on the NIST definition of cloud computing."""," In your article, use at least four subheadings to organize your content. Within each subheading, provide a new sentence that relates to the NIST definition of cloud computing.

1.Definition of Cloud Computing
2.Elasticity
3.Service
4.Resource Pooling
5.Security
6.Data Storage

 titled ""Proper Use of Cloud Computing Based on NIST Definition""

Proper Use of Cloud Computing Based on NIST Definition

1.Definition of Cloud Computing
Cloud computing is based on the concept of abstract resources that arecomprised of various services, data storage, and processing units accessed over the internet.

2.Elasticity
These services and resources can be easily scaled depending on user requirements, allowing for efficient use of computing power. This scalability elicits adynamic approach to system management.

3.Service
Users do not own these resource pools; they instead have access to them on an advocate basis, meaning they can utilize services without needing to maintain physical infrastructure.

4.Resource Pooling
The infrastructure is divided into multiple pools, including application servers, firewalls, and mail servers. This pooling of resources allows for greater efficiency and cost savings.

5.Security
Users are responsible for ensuring data security when storing information in the cloud. Cloud service providers focus on maintaining secure infrastructure to prevent unauthorized access to data.

6.Data Storage
The cloud offers users the abilitystore massive amounts of data offsite, allowing for easy access from anywhere with an internet connection. This.offsite data storage enhances disaster recovery options and reduces the risk of data loss in case of local throughfares."
"""I have scanned pages in files from hpscan001.jpg to hpscan134.jpg and want to create a single pdf including ocr. Write a command for linux console."""," To create a single PDF including OCR from scanned image files on a Linux system, you can use the tesseract OCR engine along with the pdftool command. Here's the command you can use:

```
for i in {001..134}
do
  tesseract hpscan$i.jpg hpscan$i.txt
  pdftool append - sunlight hpscan$i.txt -o output.pdf
done
```

This command loops through the image files from hpscan001.jpg to hpscan134.jpg. For each file, it uses tesseract to convert the image to a text file (hpscan$i.txt), where $i is a variable representing the file number. Then, it appends each text file to an output PDF using pdftool. The output.pdf will contain all the text from the scanned images and include OCR data."
