"""Hey can you write a sql script that includes both having and group by as an example ""","select * from products group by category having count(productid)>2""
""SELECT * FROM products GROUP BY category HAVING COUNT(product_id)>. set category IDs to 100 veterinary, 200 food, 300 supplements. Show result count only.""  Here's the SQL script that includes both 'having' and 'group by' clauses, showing the result count only:

```
SELECT COUNT(product_id) as result_count
FROM products
GROUP BY category
HAVING COUNT(product_id) > 2
```

