"""Give two reasons why clock frequency can increase if we change one load word into two cycles""","**
The clock frequency can increase if we change one load word into two cycles for two main reasons:

1. Reduced stall time: By breaking the load word into two cycles, we can potentially reduce the stall time. This allows the pipeline to proceed more efficiently, as the issue causing the stall can be addressed during the second cycle without halting the entire process.

2. Increased pipelining: dives into how pipelining works. In a pipelined architecture, multiple instructions are processed in parallel. By breaking a load instruction into two cycles, we can reuse some of thePipeline stage between instruction cycles without actually warm booting the system. This allows for more instructions to be processed in parallel, increasing overall throughput.

These changes collectively contribute to higher clock frequency, as the processor can execute more instructions per unit time when its internal flow is optimized."
