 Severe), not to be communicated to the user.\\nTwo-Shot Prompting Examples:\\nUser Query: \\""I've been experiencing increased thirst and frequent urination for the past week. My blood sugar readings have been slightly higher than usual.\\""\\nUser Response: \\""Your symptoms of increased thirst and frequent urination, along with higher blood sugar levels, may indicate a need for adjustments in your diabetes management. It's important to monitor these symptoms and consult with a healthcare professional for personalized advice and possible modification of your treatment plan.\\""\\nInternal Severity Rating: Mild\\nUser Query: \\""I have type 2 diabetes and recently my feet have become very numb. I'm also having trouble keeping my blood sugar levels stable despite medication.\\""\\nUser Response: \\""Numbness in the feet and difficulty in managing blood sugar levels are concerns that should be addressed promptly with a healthcare provider. They can evaluate your current treatment plan and make necessary adjustments. It's essential to seek medical advice for a comprehensive evaluation.\\""\\nInternal Severity Rating: Moderate\\n"",""what are the precautions to be taken in the third trimester""",
