"""I have a deeply nested json representing a python dict. The data represents files on a harddrive in the following format:\\n{\\""dir1\\"":\\n{\\""sub dir 1\\"":\\n{\\""filename\\"": {\\""bytes\\"": 123, \\""hash\\"": \\""AC3\\""},\\n\\""file2\\"": {\\""bytes\\"": 120, \\""hash\\"": \\""156\\""}\\n},\\n{\\""sub dir 2\\"":\\n{\\""file 3\\"": {\\""bytes\\"": 420, \\""hash\\"": \\""82D\\""}}\\n}}\\n\\nI want a python script that reads this deeply nested json and produces a list of files and directories in CSV format like this:\\npath, bytes, hash\\ndir1\\/sub dir 1\\/filename,123,AC3\\ndir1\\/sub dir 1\\/file2,120,156\\ndir1\\/sub dir 2\\/file 3,420,82D\\n\\nNote that the files themselfs are also dicts inside the deeply nested dict"""," The script to converter the JSON data to CSV format is:

```python
import json

# Sample JSON data
json_data = '{""dir1"": {""sub_dir 1"": {""filename"": {""bytes"": 123, ""hash"": ""AC3""}, ""file2"": {""bytes"": 120, ""hash"": ""156""}}, ""sub_dir 2"": {""file 3"": {""bytes"": 420, ""hash"": ""82D""}}}

# Function to recursively convert JSON to CSV
def json_to_csv_recursive(json_object, parent_dir=""""):
    if isinstance(json_object, dict):
        for key, value in json_object.items():
            if isinstance(value, (dict, list)):
                json_to_csv_recursive(value, parent_dir + key + '/')
            else:
                print(parent_dir + key, value['bytes'], value['hash'])
    else:
        print(parent_dir, value['bytes'], value['hash'])

# Main function
json_to_csv_recursive(json_data, '')
```

This script will print the JSON data in CSV format as requested. The parent directory is used to build the path for each file and directory in the JSON structure."
