- Fat cravings: A deficiency in healthy fats can result in rollers for high-fat foods.
- Protein cravings: A low protein intake might lead to cravings for high-protein foods.

Different nutrient deficiencies may cause cravings for different foods. For instance, deficiency in calcium may lead to a craving for dairy products. It's worth noting that excessive cravings might also be a sign of underlying health issues, so it's always a good idea to consult a healthcare professional if you're experiencing persistent cravings."
