"""I am selling an item on eBay and it is not getting any bids. What happens if the auction ends and nobody has bid on the item?"," Will I get my original fondue set back and how will I know if the item did not sell?""

In this scenario, you would get your original fondue set back. eBay's auctions are designed to close with a winning bidder, but if no one place a bid, the item simply remains listed without sale. 

To know if the item didn't sell, you'd need to check your eBay listing regularly. The auction typically lasts for a set amount of time (often 7-10 days). At the end of this period, if there's no winning bidder, eBay will automatically list your item as relisted. 

You don't lose your item by not selling it; it's your property still, and eBay just doesn't charge you for listing it once it expires. However, keep in mind that Raveness is correct that this particular fondue set isn't currently popular or in demand on eBay. You might want to consider relisting it or adjusting your price to increase its chances of selling in the future."
