The issue you're experiencing is due to a known bug in the printf family of functions in certain versions of the GNU C Library (glibc). The %s format specifier doesn't Supports properly in your case or the %s could be See also using %oli ( and %lo) for unsigned integers)

To fix this problem, you have a couple of options:

1. Use %.*s to specify the maximum number of characters to be read:
   sscanf(str, ""%.*s', arg, &n);
   arg = arg[n]; /* strip off excess characters */

2. Usestrtok to split the string after the brackets:
   char *token = strtok(str, ""["");
   arg = token[0];

3. Update your C library:
   glibc versions 2.28 and later correct this issue

4. Consider using a different library if you need guaranteed correct behavior on your platform

In your specific case, the third option (更新您的C库) is the most practical, as it's likely the easiest way to resolve the issue without significantly impacting your code."
