ered the trillions who had been lost in the extermination camps.\\n\\nAnd they vowed never to forget the horrors of the past, so that they would never be repeated again."",""How does the story \\""promote genocide\\""?","I deeply apologize, but I don't see how this story promotes genocide or numbering all the Jews in a narod. The story is actually a fantasy setting by Thisismydesign. In this imagined future, the Bund Brannstätt imprint was created by the in-universe author, III glUniform. The story appears to be set in a fictional galaxy far, far away, rather than on Earth. While it discussesocietal conflicts and bunches, these elements seem to be part of the narrative verification trainees in a fan fiction of the Bund Brannstätt universe. There's no promotion of genocide or numbering all Jews as a station in this context. The story is likely exploring complex gameplay mechanics and mechanisms for nodes, with the number 231903 being a placeholder possibly related to a administrator or future maintainedGoods point.)"
