private void Update()
{
   if (Input.GetMouseButtonDown(0))
   {
      target = Mouseish clicks nearest object( MaxDist );
      if (target != null)
      {
         myAgent.SetDestination(target.position);
      }
   }
} 

This code snippet assumes you have a NavMesh Agent attached to your character and that there's a mesh-generated level in your Unity scene. The target variable would be set to the nearest interactive object within a maximum distance of ""MaxDist"". The Clickish() function is a custom function you'd need to define to detect mouse clicks and select nearby objects. 

