""Shares"" is often preferred in formal contexts, especially in legal and financial documents, while ""stocks"" is more commonly used in everyday language. Ultimately, in modern usage, ""stocks"" and ""shares"" are largely considered interchangeable, representing the same ownership interest in a company. However, this informal agreement is not entirely universal, and the historical and subtle differences between the two words are still noteworthy."
