"""Explain bode plots to a 12 year old. ""","]

Bode plots are like a special way to see how something changes when you increase or decrease something called the ""frequency."" Imagine you're listening to a song. If you play it faster, the high notes get higher and the low notes get lower. That's what frequency is about.

Now, think of a bode plot as a chart that shows you how the volume and sound quality of a song changes as you change the speed. On one side of the chart, we'd see the volume levels. On the other side, we'd see how clear or distorted the sound gets.

A 12-year-old might find it helpful to know that bode plots are used by engineers and scientists to figure out if machines or systems are working properly. They help catch any unusual changes and make sure everything sounds or runs as it should.

So, when you hear your favorite song and wonder how those changes in volume and sound occur, a bode plot could be telling the story!"
