"""using matplotlib package and other frameworks that may be useful, Draw the tesla cybertruck from side view. Explain the basic shapes and essence of the car, think about references of the Cybertruck shape and design, make the output of the car very simple. Write down a plan first, be sure to keep track of where you\\u2019re placing shapes location, then output complete clean professional code in code compatible window."""," To create a simple side view of the Tesla Cybertruck, I'll use basic geometric shapes. Here's a plan for the code:

```python
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import numpy as np

# Set up the figure and axes
plt.figure(figsize=(6, 4))
ax = plt.gca()

# Define the main torso as a square
ax.add_patch({'xy': [40, 52], 'xy1': [36.4, 57.8], 'xy2': [44.8, 56.3], 'xy3=""51.2"", 'xy4=""46.7"", 'color=""silver""'})

# Add smaller square for fender wheel
ax.add_patch({'xy1=""40.6"", 'xy2=""74.7"", 'xy3=""46.4"", 'xy4=""70.7"", 'color=""black""'})

# Add horizontal line for wheel arch
ax.plot(np.array([[34.3, 76.5], [40.6, 76.9], [47.7, 75.8], [53.9, 76.7]], 'k')

# Add sharp edges to represent corners
ax.plot(np.array([[34.3, 71.3], [34.7, 81.0], [46.4, 82.3], [47.3, 71.5]], 'k')

# Add vertical lines for door handles
ax.plot(np.array([[36.3, 60.9], [54.4, 60.7]], 'k')

# Add simple rear view mirror
ax.plot(np.array([[40.8, 58.0]], 'k')

# Add front bumper
ax.plot(np.array([[34.7, 59.5]], 'k')

# Add back bumper
ax.plot(np.array([[46.7, 60.7]], 'k')

# Set background to white
ax.set_facecolor('white')

# Show the plot
plt.show()
```"
