"""Who was the first person to stand on the moon?"," The answer is Neil Armstrong. He became the first human to set foot on the moon on July 20, 1969, as part of NASA's Apollo 11 mission. Armstrong's historic landing coincided with the lunar module's descent to the moon's surface. As the commander of the astronauts, he is widely recognized for uttering the famous words 'One small step for man, one giant leap for mankind' as he first walked on the moon. Following Armstrong, other Apollo 11 astronauts also walked on the lunar surface. However, they were all part of the same historic mission that firmly established the moon landing as one of humanity's greatest achievements."""
