"""Analize python opencv error.\\nimgproc\\/src\\/thresh.cpp:1555: error: (-2:Unspecified error) in function 'double cv::threshold(cv::InputArray, cv::OutputArray, double, double, int)'\\n> THRESH_OTSU mode:\\n>     'src_type == CV_8UC1 || src_type == CV_16UC1'\\n> where\\n>     'src_type' is 16 (CV_8UC3)""",".

python OpenCV thresholding error occurring when using THRESH_OTSU mode. The error message suggests that the input image type is incorrect. Instead of CV_8UC3 (3-channel 8-bit unsigned integer), it should be either CV_8UC1 (1-channel 8-bit unsigned integer) or CV_16UC1 (1-channel 16-bit unsigned integer). This issue is preventing the thresholding operation from working properly in the Opencv Python interface."
