"""I'm using R, tidyverse, how do I get the color of a geom_line() to be red?",""". There are 5 possible answer options:

A) geom_point()ê疏导ex
B) theme()ê疏导ex
C) scale_color_manual(name=""Red"")
D) scale_color连续er
E) geom.line()ê疏导ex

The correct answer is C) scale_color_manual(name=""Red"")

To set the color of a geom_line() to red in R using the tidyverse package, you need to use the scale_color_manual() function. This function allows you to specify custom colors for your ggplots.

Here's a brief example:

library(tidyverse)
ggplot(data, aes(x, y)) + geom_line() + scale_color_manual(name=""Red"", color=""red"")

This code will set the color of the geom_line() to red, using the ""red"" color name that's part of the default color palette in R's ggplot2 package. The ""name"" argument is there for better readability in your code and legend."
