"""write a code about sorting"""," This code sorts a list of integers in ascending order using a selection sort algorithm. The function takes an array of integers as input and-modifies it in place to arrange the elements from smallest to largest.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void selectionSort(int arr[], int n) {
    int i, j, min_idx, temp;
    for (i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        min_idx = i;
        for (j = i+1; j < n; j++) {
            if (arr[j] < arr[min_idx]) {
                min_idx = j;
            }
        }
        temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[min_idx];
        arr[min_idx] = temp;
    }
}

int main() {
    int arr[] = {5, 3, 7, 2, 9};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
    selectionSort(arr, n);
    printf(""\\nSorted array: "");
    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        printf(""%d "", arr[i]);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

When you run this program, it will output:

```
Sorted array: 2 3 5 7 9
```

This code demonstrates the selection sort algorithm, which iteratively finds the smallest element in the unsorted portion of the array and moves it to the beginning. This process is repeated until the entire array is sorted."
