"""t-sql. round a date column with up to seconds to hours"""," The SQL query to round a date column with up to seconds to hours would be:

```
SELECT DATEPART(Step 1) + 
    DEDUCT(Step 2) FROM TableName
```

Step 1 would be replaced with ""YEAR"" if you want to round to years, ""MONTH"" for months, or ""DAY"" for days. Step 2 would be replaced with the specific time unit you want to deduct when rounding.

For example, if you want to round to the nearest hour, it might look something like this:

```
SELECT DATEPART(YEAR, DateColumn) + 
    DEDUCT(1, HOUR,后备) FROM TableName
```

This query would round the date column first to the year, then deduct 1 hour from it. If you want to round to the nearest minute, it would look like this:

```
SELECT DATEPART(YEAR, DateColumn) + 
    DEDUCT(0, HOUR, 60) FROM TableName
```

Of course, you should replace ""TableName"" with your actual table name, and ""DateColumn"" with your specific date column name."
