"""In Microsoft Word, how do I get citations in the format Author (2020)?","""

To achieve citations in the format Author (2020) in Microsoft Word, you'll need to use the built-in citation and reference system. Here's how to do it:

1. Click on the ""Insert"" tab at the top of the Word document.

2. In the ""Insert"" ribbon, look for the ""Citation & Reference"" section. It's typically represented by a button with a small book icon.

3. Click on the ""Citation & Reference"" button. This will open adialog box with various citation options.

4. In the dialog box, select the style that closely matches your preferred format. For your specific question, look for a style that includesthe author's name followed by the publication year in parentheses.

5. Choose a citation format that includes the author's name and year, such as ""Author (2020)"" or "" author yearelif:"".

6. Click on ""Select"" to apply the chosen style to your document.

7. As you type your document, you'll see small, numbered footnotes appear next to the relevant sources. These footnotes can later be transformed into in-text citations.

8. When you're ready, click on the ""Referencing Style"" button to choose which biblert Disklusion style you want to use for your references.

Remember, once you set up your preferred format in Microsoft Word, it'll bemuch easier to use this system throughout your document, ensuring consistent and accurate citations.

If you need further guidance or have additional questions about citationing in Word, feel free to ask."
