"""wt is rail to rail"""," means width rail to rail is the total distance between the outer edges of the two rails that the train sits on.

This measurement is crucial for understanding the physical dimensions of a railway track. It directly impacts train design, rail credits, and the overall capacity of the railway system.

The exact width varies depending on the specific track gauges used, but common standards include 1,435 mm (4,900,000th mm) or 1,600 mm (600,000th mm) for standard gauge railways.

For example, a 1,600 mm gauge railway would publicize its rail to rail width as ""1,600 mm"" (or 600,000th mm). The ""mm"" denotes millimeters, which is the standard unit for measuring such precise breadths.

This measurement is vital for railway engineers, designers, and operators to ensuring compatibility and safety across different railway systems."
