The Canadian system shares some similarities with the UK's cabinet责任制, but it has its own distinct terminology and implementation. Both systems recognize the importance of collective decision-making and public support within cabinets, though they may approach this differently in practice.

This concept is crucial in both Canadian and UK governance, serving as a foundation for a strong, cohesive executive branch accountable to parliament or the House of Commons, respectively."
