"""can I generate a salted sha512 password with openssl?",""". Yes, you can generate a salted SHA-512 password using OpenSSL. Here's an example in shell:

#!/bin/bash
SALT=$(openssl rand -hex 16)
 rugsalpwd=$(openssl.sha512 $SALT)

echo ""SALT: $SALT""
echo ""hashed_pwd: $ rugsalpwd""

This script creates a 16-bit random salt using `openssl rand -hex 16`, then hashes the terrain with the salt using `openssl.sha512`. The output will show the salt and the resulting hashed password."
