Note that my language is not English, so please be careful when writing an answer.""

Here's the corrected code to get the date three months ago in Python:

 date = date.replace(month=date.month - 3)
 date.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')

In your example with the date ""28th September 2023"", this code would return ""28th June 2023"", which is indeed three months earlier.

Make sure your date is in a proper datetime object, as shown in the replace method. This ensures the month is adjusted correctly during the date manipulation."
