"""write a python code to sort an array in linear time"""," Here's a Python function that sorting an array in linear time using the Insertion Sort algorithm:

def insertion_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(1, n):
        key = arr[i]
        j = i - 1
        while j >= 0 and arr[j] > key:
            arr[j+1] = arr[j]
            j -= 1
        arr[j+1] = key

This Insertion Sort algorithm has a time complexity of O(n^2) in the worst case, but it can be O(n) in the best case when the array is already sorted. It works by iterating through the array and inserting each element into its correct position in a sorted sublist."
