You see, long ago, our ancestors were very smart! They lived in big teams called tribes. One day, one of the tribe leaders fell sick and wasn't getting better. 

So, they decided to try something special. They built a big hole and put the sick leader in it. But they didn't stop there. They put something called a coffin on top of the leader. 

Now, when we bury someone, we put them in special underground rooms with some interesting things. We put very important things like gold coins and nice weapons in these rooms with the leader. 

This is called baptism. It's like giving the leader something important as they go to sleep forever.

So, these smart people buried their big leaders to keep them safe and have something special to look for when they find them again.

And that's why we see big holes in the ground sometimes. That's where we put very important people when they're no longer with us.

Isn't that cool? They were kind of like detectives, trying to figure out how to keep the leader safe and another leader in the future!"
