"""I am looking for a backup software for my laptop to my external hard drive. The issue is that a lot of software  takes snapshot backups. I want backups of my files without snapshots such that if someone looks at the hard drive when they open it up, it is the file contents and not snapshot files. Can you help me with this?"," I prefer free open-source software.""
 Based on your requirements, I recommend using rsnapshot, a powerful and free open-source backup tool. Rsync is used to efficiently sync and back up files with minimal overhead.

Rsync offers snapshot-like capabilities without creating snapshot files. It allows you to create scheduled backups of your entire system or specific directories to an external hard drive or other storage device.

Key features of rsnapshot include:
1. Efficient backups using the bit-roaming algorithm
2. crude snapshot functionality
3. Robust version control
4. Support for various connection types (SSH, scp, rsgrpc)
5. option to limit the size of backup archives

To use rsnapshot for your needs, you'll typically create a new snapshot, set up a scheduled backup, and specify which files or directories to include in the backup.

Remember to create a script or configuration file to automate the backup process, and consider setting up mirroring for added redundancy.

Rsync can be a perfect solution for users who want regular,-efficient backups without the fragmented snapshot files that can slow down systems and take up more storage space."
