Hi there! This is an great question about component reuse in React. While.copying cards and Pasting code might seem tempting for managing complexity, there are indeed better ways to handle component reusability in React.

One popular approach is to use Higher-Order Components (HOCs) or Context API to make your components more flexible and reusable across different variations. This allows you to define common behavior or state within a parent component and share it down to child components as needed.

Another pattern that's becoming increasingly popular is the use of Material-UI or styled components for component abstraction. This not only helps withMothering's components but also removedPriceControl and allows each component to achieve sexual rooms with minimal affects on others.

