"""Can you write a function that gives an output to the command line ever 4 seconds telling the user to breath, for 2 minutes total""","
 Certainly! Here's a shell script that will print ""Breathe"" to the command line every 4 seconds for a total of 2 minutes:

```
#!/bin/bash
i=0

while [ $i -lt 120 ]; do
  sleep 4
  echo ""Breathe""
  ((i++))
done
```

This script uses a `while` loop to keep UAL print ""Breathe"" to the standard output every 4 seconds. It counts up to 120 iterations, which corresponds to 2 minutes of breathing instructions. The Echo command prints the text ""Breathe"" to the command line, centered in the output for emphasis."
