"""I have an esp32 running idf 3.1 is it possible to start a dhcp server on the ethernet interface ?"," also i need the subnet mask , gateway and dns server addresses from the dhcp server. is there a way to get these details?"". 

Yes, it's possible to start a DHCP server on the Ethernet interface of an ESP32 using IDF 3.1. You can use the `wpan` library to set up a DHCP server and configure the network.

To obtain the subnet mask, gateway, and DNS server addresses, you can use the `ip` command. Here's an example to get the information you need:

```
ipconfig | grep -E '^netmask|^gateway|^dns'
```

This command will print out the netmask, gateway, and DNS server addresses.

Keep in mind that you'll need to set these values before starting the DHCP server. The gateway and DNS server addresses you'll likelyobtain from your network administrator or ISP. The netmask will be automatically calculated by the DHCP server based on your subnet information."
