   - Use batch-sized pinned memory for optimal performance
   - Dispose of `torch.device` objects when done to free GPU memory

2. Common GPU-related errors and their solutions:
   - `OOM (Out of Memory)` errors:
     - Reduce batch size
     - Use PyTorch's memory fragmentationaware version (`.set_memory_fraction` on DataLoader)
     - Increase swap lifecycle.median to allow more memory usage
   - `CUDA out of range error`:
     - Ensure your torch version supports the requested CUDA version
     - Check if your GPU Melbourne has the required CUDA capabilities
