   a. deliverance from sin's penalty (Romans 6:23)
   b. placement in God's family (John 1:12)
   c. new life by the Holy Spirit (John 10:10)

II. How do I Obtain Salvation?
   a. through faith alone in Jesus Christ (Ephesians 2:8-9)
   b. no works required (Galatians 2:16)
   c. received as a gift (Ephesians 2:10)

III. What does Saved Mean?
   a. forgiven of all sins (1 John 1:9)
   b. guaranteed eternal life (John 10:28)
   c. dramatic spiritual transformation (2 Corinthians 5:17)

IV. How does Salvation Affect Daily Life?
   a. fills with joy and purpose (Galatians 5:22-23)
   b. enables following Jesus' teachings (Matthew 5:13-16)
   c. connects us to a community of believers (Acts 2:42)

V. Common Misconceptions
   a. Saved = go to heaven (1 Thessalonians 4:13-17)
   b.rocket science (Romans 8:14-17)

VI. Final Thoughts
   a. CEPLA podcast Starting Soon
   b. Google Meet Upcoming
   c. bring renewal materials

