"""bjbjbjkbkj"",""what is the cause of sturge weber syndrome?",""". 10 lines of text about sturge weber syndrome, shorter lines if possible.

 Sturge-Weber syndrome (SWS) is a genetic disorder characterized by facial and mural (tissue) coloration, particularly on the left side. It is caused by a mutation in the GNAO1 gene, which encodes a subunit of G Protein alpha-O NOTCH2L complex.

SWS occurs when there's a gain of function mutation in GNAO1, leading to uncontrolled Gαq activity and subsequent neurodevelopmental abnormalities.

The syndrome is most commonly associated with port-wine stains (blush marks) and hemangiomas on the face, especially on the left side. It can also affect other parts of the body, including the brain, resulting in cerebral partial hemisclerosis.

Most individuals with SWS experience visual impairments due to- dilations of the frontalis muscle, hemispherical cortical blindness (pseudowneurosthenia), or占位性病变 in thegrey matter.

It's important to note that the cause and etiology of SWS remain the same-一个 Southwest genetic mutation. The symptoms and severity can vary widely among affected individuals.

