"""A dish of sugar water was left on a window sill. One week later, there were only sugar crystals left in the dish. The water was gone. The best explanation for the appearance of sugar crystals is (A) some of the water was absorbed by the dish. (B) the air condensed. (C) the light shining on the window sill produced more sugar. (D) the water evaporated."""," clustered evaporation.

The correct answer is D) the water evaporated.

When water evaporates, it leaves behind the dissolved substances, in this case, sugar. As the water vapor rises into the air and cools, it can condense, forming clouds or dew. However, the description states that there are sugar crystals left in the dish, not any visible water condensation on the window sill.

Option A is incorrect because the total amount of water didn't change; it simply evaporated, leavingBehind dissolved sugar. Option B is also wrong as there's no mention of any visible condensation. Option C is not a plausible explanation for sugar crystals in a dish, as it would require light shining on the window sill to produce additional sugar in the water."
