"""What is the Gaia space telescope?"," A upgrade to the Hubble space telescope?""

The Gaia space telescope is indeed an upgrade to the Hubble space telescope, but it's more than just an improvement. Gaia is a 

欧空局和美国国家航空航天局合作 ESA–NASA Gaia project that launched in 2013. It's designed to provide a detailed 3D map of our local section of the Milky Way galaxy.

Gaia's main instruments are a camera and a precise colorometer. It can measure the positions and colors of stars with incredible accuracy. So far, Gaia has cataloged millions of stars, planets (including some Earth-like ones), and other celestial objects in our galaxy.

While both Gaia and Hubble are used for astronomical research, Gaia's primary goal is to create a comprehensive catalog of our galaxy's stars, while Hubble is focused more on deep field observations and studying individual celestial objects."
