"""among japanese horses, which 10 have won the most g1 races"""," shows a table with 5 horse names listed. how many more g1 races can the top 10 horses win if they each won 1 more race? 50

The top 10 Japanese horses have won 50 G1 races in total. If each horse won 1 more race, there would be an additional 10 races won by the top 10. Therefore, the total number of G1 races that could be won by the top 10 horses if they each won 1 more race would be 50 (current total) + 10 (additional races) = 60 races."
