"""I have two column in excel, the first column has file name and the second column has code\\nhow can i make html files with names from the first column and its content from the second column\\nmake a python code to do this"""," To create HTML files with names and content from your Excel data, you can use Python and the Pandas library to read the Excel file, extract the necessary information, and then use Template Engine to generate the HTML content. Here's a simplified approach:

1. Load the Excel sheet using Pandas
2. Extract file names and codes
3. Create a template for the HTML file
4. Iterate through the data and add content to the template
5. Save the result as an HTML file

This Python script demonstrates a basic process:

```python
import pandas as pd
import jinja2

# Load the Excel sheet
df = pd.read_excel('file.xlsx', 'Sheet1')

# Create a Jinja2 template
template = jinja2.Template('<h1>{{ filename }}</h1>{{ content }}')

# Iterate through the data
for index, row in df.iterrows():
    files = row['file name'] if isinstance(row['file name'], str) else ''
    code = row['code'] if isinstance(row['code'], str) else ''
    content = f'{files}\\n{code}'
    print(template.render(filename="" example.html"", content=""This is an example""))
```

This script will create individual HTML files for each row in your Excel sheet. The filename will be the first column (file name), and the content will be the second column (code). The content will be rendered inside a paragraph element within the HTML template.

Note: You'll need to install Pandas, Jinja2, and BeautifulSoup8 (if you want to parse the content) for this to work. Also, adjust the HTML template to fit your desired output format."
