Sun Yatsen's contributions to San Francisco were significant, particularly during his exile in the city from 1905 to 1907. During this time, he used the city as a base to organize and plan his revolutionary activities. His efforts in San Francisco played a crucial role in his eventual return to China and his actions that led to the foundation of the Republic of China in 1912.

