"""Write a simple Java program for a calculator that can understand and display fractions and does simple calculation of plus, minus, divide, muluply."""," Here's a Java program for a simple calculator that can understand and display fractions and Perform basic operations like addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division:

```java
import fractions.Fraction;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Calculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        while (true) {
            System.out.println(""\\nEnter fraction in the format: a/b"");
            System.out.print(""First fraction: "");
            Fraction first = scanner.nextFraction();
            System.out.print(""Operator: "");
            String operator = scanner.next();
            System.out.print(""Second fraction: "");
            Fraction second = scanner.nextFraction();

            switch (operator) {
                case ""+"":
                    Fraction result = first.add(second);
                    System.out.println(""Result: "" + result);
                    break;
                case ""-"":
                    result = first.subtract(second);
                    System.out.println(""Result: "" + result);
                    break;
                case ""*"":
                    result = first.multiply(second);
                    System.out.println(""Result: "" + result);
                    break;
                case ""/"":
                    if (second.denominator == 0) {
                        System.out.println("" Division by zero! "");
                        break;
                    }
                    result = first.divide(second);
                    System.out.println(""Result: "" + result);
                    break;
                default:
                    System.out.println(""Unknown operator. Please use +, -, *, or /."");
                    break;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This program uses the fractions library to handle fractional numbers. It prompts the user to enter two fractions and an operator between them. The main loop continues until a zero denominator is encountered or the user decides to stop.

The program handles addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division of fractions. It also provides feedback for unknown operators, division by zero errors, and displays the results of each operation."
