"""write one-liner fizzbuzz in Rust."""," Here's a cleanliness-optimized one-liner fizzbuzz function in Rust:

```rust
fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) {
    (1..n).enumerate()
        .filter_map(|(i, x)| if i%3==0 {Some(""Fizz"")} else if i%5==0 {Some(""Buzz"")}`
        .filter(|x| x!="""").flatten().collect::<Vec<String>>()
        .join(""\\n"")
}
```

This function takes a usize argument representing the number of terms in the sequence. It maps each number from 1 to n-1 to either ""Fizz"", ""Buzz"", or """" based on the value of i modulo 3 and i modulo 5. It filters out any empty strings, flattens the resulting Vec<String>, and join it into a single string separated by newlines."
