"""Can radio signals travel faster than light?"," Specifically, does FM radio travel faster than light?""

Yes, radio signals, including FM radio, indeed travel faster than light. This is due to the nature of electromagnetic waves, of which radio waves are a part.

Light and all other electromagnetic waves, including radio waves, move at the speed of light in a vacuum. This speed is approximately 299,792,458 meters per second (or about 186,282 miles per second).

The velocity of electromagnetic waves, including FM radio, is accordingly c (the speed of light)."
