"""write a bash script that will run the command \\""jamf recon;jamf policy\\"" only if the current ip address starts with 192.168 or 10.1"""," This bash script will run the specified commands if the current IP address begins with either 192.168 or 10.1:

#!/bin/bash

# Check IP address
current_ip=$(ip -c-link | grep -o 'inet' | awk '{print $1}')
ip_prefix=$(current_ip | cut -d':' -f3)

# Define network ranges
192.168_net=""192.168.0.0/24""
10.1_net=""10.1.0.0/32""

# Determine if IP is within specified networks
if [ ""$ip_prefix"" = ""192.168"" ]; then
    jamf recon | jamf policy
elif [ ""$ip_prefix"" = ""10.1"" ]; then
    jamf recon | jamf policy
else
    # IP not within specified networks
    echo ""IP address not matching expected range""
fi

This script uses `ip` command to get the current IP address, extracts the network prefix, and compares it against defined network ranges using if-else statements. If the IP matches either range, it executes the `jamf recon` and `jamf policy` commands. If not, it prints a message indicating the IP does not match the expected range."
