"""how to automatically store and load wpf settings from a finished settings page?","""
To automatically store and load WPF settings, you can use the ConfigurationService class provided by the FriendsOfWPF library. Here's a simplified approach:

1. Install the FriendsOfWPF.Configuration NuGet package.

2. Create a Configuration class with your settings:
   public class Configuration {
     public string My setting { get; set; }
   }

3. In your main window, register the configuration:
   App.Current ConfigurationService = new ConfigurationService();

4. Set or retrieve settings:
   ConfigurationService.Configuration.My Setting = ""New value"";
   string mySetting = ConfigurationService.Configuration.My Setting;

5. To persist settings, call ConfigurationService.Save().
   // This will store the settings in App.Config or a file in your project directory.

This method allows easy handling of WPF settings both locally and in production environments, providing automatic storage and loading capabilities."
