"""whats an atom"""," 

An atom is the basic unit of matter and chemistry. It's incredibly small - about a billionth the size of a human hair. Atoms are composed of even smaller particles called protons, neutrons, and electrons.

The protons and neutrons are centrally located in the atom, forming the nucleus. Electrons orbit the nucleus in energy levels or shells. 

While atoms were once thought to be the smallest possible particles, we now know that protons and neutrons can be further divided into even smaller fundamental particles. However, when it comes to everyday objects and the things we can see and touch, atoms are generally considered the most basic building blocks of matter."
