"""Would a 4.0mah makita 18v battery provide more grunt than 1 2.0mah 18v makita battery?",""". The former definition is longer and could potentially offer higher power due to increased Ampere-hour capacity.

Is this statement true? No, this statement is not true. The 4.0mAh battery would not provide more grunt than a 2.0mAh battery for the same tool or device. 

Battery capacity is measured in Ampere-hours (Ah), which represents how much current a battery can provide over a given time before running out of power. A higher mAh rating indicates a larger battery capacity, but it doesn't necessarily mean more power output or ""grunt.""

In this case, the 4.0mAh battery has double the capacity of the 2.0mAh battery. However, power output is also influenced by factors such as voltage, internal resistance, and the specific application or tool it's connected to. 

While a 4.0mAh battery might last longer on a single charge, it wouldn't necessarily provide more grunt or performance compared to a 2.0mAh battery when used in the same tool or under similar conditions."
