"""What's the purpose of the sensitivity list in VHDL processes?","""
The sensitivity list in VHDL processes serves as a set of ports or signals that determine when a process should be sensitive to changes. It tells the compiler which signals need to be watched for edges (的变化) or levels (的状态) that might trigger the process to execute. This allows VHDL to optimize the code by only simulating the process when it's actually needed, wing and reduced the search space for simulation."
