"""Which is heavier, a kilogram of bricks, or a kilogram of feathers?"," why?""

This is a trick question designed to make the reader think about units of weight rather than the objects themselves. A kilogram is a fixed unit of mass, regardless of what substance it's measuring. So while bricks and feathers may have different volumes, they both weigh the same amount when measured in kilograms.

