"""explain meta learning """," Meta_learning, also known as ""learning to learn,"" is an advanced Machine Learning concept that extends beyond traditional supervised learning. It involves training models to learn from data"" - Machine Learning MasterSTudent

Meta_learning allows learners to adapt quickly to new tasks by using information from related tasks. This is achieved through a ""learning-to-learn"" architecture, where a separate metalearner or ""coach"" is trained to guide the main learner.

In essence,(meta learning) enables the model to identify patterns and transfer knowledge across related tasks, making it highly efficient in learning new things with minimal data and quick convergence.

The core idea is to develop generalizable representations that can be applied to various tasks, rather than learning fixed models for each specific scenario. This approach enhances the model's adaptability and robustness in real-world applications where data may be scarce or rapidly changing.

1. Task representation networks
2. Memory buffer of previous tasks
