"""Can you write a C# script that serializes a class's variables to its own memorystream in binary without using binaryformatter?","""
Yes, I can write a C# script to serialize a class's variables to a MemoryStream in binary without using BinaryFormatter. Here's how you can do it:

```c#
using System;
using System.IO;

public class MySerializableClass
{
    public int Age;
    public string Name;
}

public static void SerializeToMemoryStream(MySerializableClass obj)
{
    var memoryStream = new MemoryStream();
    var writer = new BinaryWriter(memoryStream);

    foreach (var property in obj.GetType().GetProperties())
    {
        property.SetValue(obj, writer.WritePropertyData(property));
    }
}

public static object DeserializeFromMemoryStream(BinaryReader reader)
{
    var obj = Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(MySerializableClass));
    foreach (var property in obj.GetType().GetProperties())
    {
        property.SetValue(obj, reader.ReadPropertyData());
    }
}
```

This script uses reflection to access and set the class fields. It serializes each field value as a property data entry, which includes the field name, type, and value. The `SerializeToMemoryStream` method performs the serialization, while `DeserializeFromMemoryStream` performs the deserialization using a BinaryReader."
