"""How can I create the campfire effect on unreal-engine using niagara particles?","We want to use the material itself together with a particle system."" To create a campfire effect using Unreal Engine and Niagara particles, you can follow these steps:

1. Set up a Niagara particle system in your scene.

2. Inside the particle system, add a material with a flame texture. This will serve as the base for your campfire.

3. Add a colored particle effect to the system. Use a warm color like orange or yellow to represent flames.

4. Adjust the emission rate and lifetime of the colored particles to control their density and how long they last.

5. Use Niagara particles' lifetime attributes to make the flames appear to flicker and dance.

6. Add a particle texture baker to the material to create realistic smoke.

7. Adjust advanced settings like particle size, velocity, and attraction forces to get the desired campfire effect.

8. position decals to represent embers and ashes if desired.

