"""Write a recursive function in erlang"""," This is a simple Erlang function that calculates the sum of numbers from 1 to n using recursion:

```erlang
sum(n) ->
    if n == 1 then
        1
    else
        n + sum(n-1)
    end.
```

This function uses mathematical induction to work its way down to 1, adding each number as it goes. When called, it will recursively sum all integers from 1 up to whatever value of n you provide.

Erlang is well-suited for handling concurrency with its message passing model, but this particular example of recursion is straightforward and unrelated to concurrent programming."
