"""A water tank has a square base with a side length of 10 feet. If the water level is 5 feet deep, how many gallons of water are in the tank?"," (1 cubic foot = 7.48 gallons) The tank is filled from the bottom.)""
To solve this problem, we need to calculate the volume of water in the tank and then convert it to gallons.

Step 1: Calculate the volume of water
Volume = length × width × depth
Volume = 10 feet × 10 feet × 5 feet = 500 cubic feet

Step 2: Convert cubic feet to gallons
500 cubic feet × 7.48 gallons/cubic foot = 3,740 gallons

Therefore, there are 3,740 gallons of water in the tank."
"""Rewrite this script using python. Replace the argument handling using argparse. Remove the --help argument. The other two arguments are both optional and can be passed at the same time or separately.\\nMake sure to stick to the official python style guides and use a main() function.\\n```\\ncopy_firefox=0\\n\\n# handle arguments\\nif [[ \\""$#\\"" -eq 1 ]]; then\\n    # -t\\/--theme to change theme\\n    if [[ \\""$1\\"" == \\""-t\\"" || \\""$1\\"" == \\""--theme\\"" ]]; then\\n        func_seltheme\\n    elif [[ \\""$1\\"" == \\""-f\\"" || \\""$1\\"" == \\""--firefox\\"" ]]; then\\n        copy_firefox=1\\n    elif [[ \\""$1\\"" == \\""-h\\"" || \\""$1\\"" == \\""--help\\"" ]]; then\\n        echo \\""-h, --help     Show help menu\\""\\n        echo \\""-t, --theme    Show theme selection screen\\""\\n        echo \\""-f, --firefox  Update firefox config\\""\\n        exit 0\\n    fi\\nelif [[ \\""$#\\"" -gt 1 ]]; then\\n    echo \\""Too many arguments\\""\\n    exit 1\\nfi\\n```"""," Here's the Python code based on the provided script, following the official Python style guides and using argparse for argument handling:

