4. Social awareness: humans twisting centrally their most advanceable capability, enables complex social互动 and relationships, while most tiranish animals have more limited social circles.

In conclusion, while animals and humans share some aspects of self-awareness, the operation of reflexive self-consciousness differs significantly between the two. The human brain, through millions of years of evolution, has developed complex cognitive structures that allow for unprecedented self-reflection and introspection, setting us apart from most other species on our planet."
