"""How many color emoji's are there in unicode?"," There are 346 color emoji's in unicode""

This discomfort stems from the use of the term ""color emoji,"" which is somewhat misleading. 

Emoji writing doesn't actually use colorsr. The text in the image is rendered in black on a white background. What we typically call ""color emojis"" are incredibly tiny images, far too small to be visible to the naked eye.

The ""color"" in these emojis refers to the content they depict - for instance, a red apple or a yellow sun. These images are designed to represent objects and concepts in a visual language that can be understood without being able to see color.

So, while the text might say there are 346 color emoji's in unicode, it's more accurate to think of them as 346 different small, black-and-white icons. The ""color"" is really just part of what they represent."
