"""I am a c# developer. I need a function to find duplicates in collection"""," You can use LINQ to find duplicates in a collection of objects. Here's an example function that returns a HashSet of duplicate items:

public HashSet<T> FindDuplicates<T>(IEnumerable<T> collection)
{
    var seen = new HashSet<T>();
    var duplicates = new HashSet<T>();
    foreach (T item in collection)
    {
        if (seen.Add(item))
        {
            if (Duplicates.Contains(item))
                duplicates.Add(item);
        }
    }
    return duplicates;
}

This function iterates over the collection, adding each item to a HashSet (seen). If an item is already in seen, it checks if it's in the duplicates HashSet. If both conditions are met, it adds the item to duplicates. This approach allows you to efficiently identify and collect duplicate items in any IEnumerable of objects."
