"""create a generic java method that wait for a contition with a max number of tentative"""," Here's a generic Java method that waits for a condition to be met with a maximum number of tentative attempts:

public static <T> void waitForCondition(
    T object, 
    Predicate<T> predicate, 
    long maxTries, 
    long interval) {
    long tries = 0;
    while (!predicate.test(object)) {
        try {
            Thread.sleep(interval);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
        if (++tries > maxTries) {
            throw new TimeoutException(""Exceeded maximum number of tries"");
        }
    }
}

This method takes a generic object, a predicate to check, a maximum number of tries, and an interval between attempts. It will repeatedly call the predicate on the object, sleeping between attempts, until the predicate returns true or until the maximum number of tries is reached. If the predicate never returns true or if the try count exceeds the maximum, it will throw a TimeoutException."
