"""Develop a C++ program that reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file."""," Here's a C++ program that reads a text file line by line and counts the occurrences of a specific word:

#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

int main() {
    std::ifstream file(""input.txt"");
    std::string word, line;
    int count = 0;
    
    if (file.is_open()) {
        while (std::getline(file, line)) {
            std::cout << line << std::endl;
            std::cout.flush();
            
            std::size_t pos = line.find(""world"");
            if (pos != std::string::npos) {
                count++;
            }
        }
    }
    else {
        std::cerr << ""Error: Could not open input file 'input.txt'"" << std::endl;
        return 1;
    }
    
    std::cout << ""Count of 'world': "" << count << std::endl;
    return 0;
}

This program opens a file called ""input.txt"" and reads each line individually. It then searches for the word ""world"" within each line using the `find` method. If the word is found, it increments the Count variable. Finally, it prints the total count of occurrences."
