"""I am writing a code in bash for rofi. tell me how to change window width and height"""," To change the window width and height in the rofi terminal, you can use the ""-w"" and ""-h"" options respectively.

For example:

rofi -w 800 -h 600

This will set the rofi window to 800 pixels wide and 600 pixels high.

If you want to make these changes dynamic, you might want to add them to your ~/.dot-rofi file. You could use a function like this:

rofi() {
  local width=${W/ic}
  local height=${H/ic}
  if [ -n ""$width"" -and -n ""$height"" ]; then
    rofi -w $width -h $height
  else
    rofi
  fi
}

This function will check if width and height variables are set before passing them to rofi. If they are not set, it will fall back to the default rofi behavior."
