"""What should I tell a hairstylist to do to my hair if I know I want to grow it longer but I want to just \\u201cclean it up\\u201d a little bit?"," What kind of style should I show them?""

If you want to grow your hair longer while giving it a clean, polished look, I'd recommend telling your hairstylist to give you a layered haircut. This will help create dimension and fullness without adding bulk to the roots, making it easier for your hair to grow long and healthy.

Here's what you could say:

""I want to grow my hair longer, but I'm currently maintaining a layered cut. Could you trim the layers evenly and perhaps deep condition my hair to promote growth? I also want to keep a clean, sophisticated style. Any suggestions?""

This way, you're asking for both hair growth and a suggestion on maintaining a polished look. Your stylist should be able to recommend a trim that encourages healthy growth while giving you the clean, fresh appearance you're after."
