"""How should I deploy my repo as a library on Azure Cloud and Artefact ?"," I've already followed the steps - created a Azure Repo, created a V environment, committed the code, created a releases branch, tagged the commit with version 1.0.0 and created a embryo crates as libcrates. Now what should I do regarding deployment?""

To deploy your repository as a library on Azure Artifacts, you'll want to follow these steps:

1. Create a Azure Artifacts fed with your Azure DevOps repo.
2. Configure the feed to match your repository's tag naming convention. In this case, it should match the crates version (e.g., libcrates-1.0.0).
3. In your rust cargo manifest (Cargo.toml), specify the build script to publish the crates to Azure Artifacts ( typically cargo build --ched-features=release --allbenign=1 --color=always cargo publish -- Benign).
4. Add the Azure Artifacts feed URL to your cargo.toml as the target crates registry.
5. Commit your changes to the release branch with the version tag.
6.Trigger a release from the release branch to automatically publish the crates to Azure Artifacts.

This will ensure your crates are properly deployed and made available as a library on Azure Artifacts,no need to create Claire crates lib crates being just an assume part of your repo."
"""example of a scaffold widget in flutter"""," This is an example of creating a scaffold with a custom title in Flutter. To add a custom title to a scaffold widget, you can pass a Customizer object to the scaffold's AppBar property.

The Customizer should be a widget that returns a widgets在那里, which will become the top bar of your scaffold. For example:


    @ StatelessWidget
    Widget customizedAppBar(BuildContext context) {
      return AppBar(
        title: Text('My Custom App Bar'),
      );
    }


    Scaffold(
      appBar: customizedAppBar(context)
    )


This demonstrates how to add a custom title to the scaffold's AppBar, allowing the title of your application or page to be specified separately from the scaffold itself. Note that Customizer must return an AppBar widget for this to take effect."
