"""please provide a 3 months detailed training to let me reach 10 km run under 1 hour. At the moment, I'm able to run 5 km in 40 minutes, then I need rest. Explain each training session in details."""," Certainly! I'll provide you with a 3-month detailed training plan to help you achieve your goal of running 10 km in under 1 hour. This plan will build up your endurance and speed gradually over time. Here's a detailed breakdown of each training session for the next 3 months:

Month 1 (Week 1-4):
1. Week 1:
   - Monday: Easy run: 3 km at 6:30 min/km pace
   - Wednesday: Strength training: Focus on core and lower body exercises
   - Friday: Long run: 5 km at 7:00 min/km pace
   - Sunday: Rest day

2. Week 2:
   - Monday: Interval training: 4 x 1 km at 5:45 min/km, 2 min rest
   - Wednesday: tempos: 6 x 200m at 5:00 min/200m
   - Friday: Long run: 6 km at 7:30 min/km pace
   - Sunday: Rest day

3. Week 3:
   - Monday: Tempo run: 8 km at 6:50 min/km
   - Wednesday: Speed work: 4 x 400m at 3:30 min/400m
   - Friday: Long run: 7 km at 7:45 min/km pace
   - Sunday: Rest day

4. Week 4:
   - Monday: Hill sprints: 4 x 500m uphill at 7:00 min/500m downhill
   - Wednesday: Long run: 8 km at 8:00 min/km pace
   - Friday: Interval training: 6 x 150m at 6:00 min/150m
   - Sunday: Rest day

Month 2 (Week 5-8):
1. Week 5:
   - Monday: Long run with zones: 5 km at Zone 2 (7:15 min/km)
   - Wednesday: Strength training: Focus on hip flexors and腿部
   - Friday: Interval training: 4 x 1 km at 5:30 min/km, 2 min rest
   - Sunday: Rest day

2. Week 6:
   - Monday: Long run: 6 km at Zone 2 (7:20 min/km)
   - Wednesday: tempos: 6 x 200m at 5:30 min/200m
   - Friday: Strength training: Focus on core and upper body
   - Sunday: Rest day

3. Week 7:
   - Monday: Interval training: 8 x 500m at 5:15 min/500m
   - Wednesday: Speed work: 4 x 400m at 3:20 min/400m
   - Friday: Long run: 7 km at Zone 2 (7:30 min/km)
   - Sunday: Rest day

4. Week 8:
   - Monday: Hill sprints: 4 x 500m uphill at Zone 3 (7:45 min/500m downhill)
   - Wednesday: Long run with zones: 8 km at Zone 2 (7:40 min/km)
   - Friday: Interval training: 6 x 150m at 5:00 min/150m
   - Sunday: Rest day

Month 3 (Week 9-12):
1. Week 9:
   - Monday: Long run with zones: 10 km at Zone 2 (7:50 min/km)
   - Wednesday: Strength training: Focus on plyometrics and upper body
   - Friday: Interval training: 4 x 2 km at 5:50 min/2 km
   - Sunday: Rest day

2. Week 10:
   - Monday: Long run: 11 km at Zone 2 (7:60 min/km)
   - Wednesday: tempos: 7 x 200m at 5:45 min/200m
   - Friday: Speed work: 4 x 400m at 3:30 min/400m
   - Sunday: Rest day

3. Week 11:
   - Monday: Interval training: 8 x 500m at 6:00 min/500m
   - Wednesday: Strength training: Focus on core and lower body
   - Friday: Long run: 8 km at Zone 2 (7:35 min/km)
   - Sunday: Rest day

4. Week 12:
   - Monday: Hill sprints: 4 x 500m uphill at 7:15 min/500m downhill
   - Wednesday: Long run with zones: 10 km at Zone 2 (7:45 min/km)
   - Friday: Interval training: 6 x 150m at 5:15 min/150m
   - Sunday: Rest day

This 3-month training plan will include a mix of long runs, speed work, interval training, and strength training to build your endurance and speed gradually. Remember to gradually increase your mileage and intensity as the weeks progress. Listen to your body and rest when needed. Good luck with your training!"
