"""When is the Fisher Information matrix equal to the Hessian?"," Are there any examples of distributions where this occurs?""

The Fisher Information matrix and the Hessian are equal for additively separable models. A common example is the Gaussian distribution, where both matrices reduce to the variance-covariance matrix. 

More broadly, this equivalence occurs in exponential family distributions, including the Gaussian, Poisson, and Gamma distributions."
