"""What tense is commonly used in deep learning papers in the methods section or equivalent?"," The past perfect tense is the one that is commonly used. The past perfect tense is commonly used in scientific papers, including deep learning papers. It is particularly useful for describing tasks or experiments that were completed before the current study began. This tense allows researchers to clearly distinguish between their current research and the work of others, while also providing a timeline of events that led to their study. The past perfect tense is especially effective in methods sections, where it helps to create a clear narrative of the research process."""
