void FixedUpdate(): Called at a fixed rate, unaffected by frame rate. Use this for physical simulations or late-game update tasks.

void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other):Called when a physics collides with this object. Use this for handling collisions.

void OnTriggerStay(): Called every frame while the object isMinimum stay in the trigger.Use this for objects that need to be constantly comparison.

void OnCollisionEnter(Collision other): Called when an initial physics collision occurs. Use this for handling	first impact.

void OnCollisionStay(): Called every frame while the object is in a collision. Use this for objects that need to responds to ongoing collisions.

void late Update(): Called after Update but before FixedUpdate. Use this for late-game update tasks that need to run after physics simulations.

IEnumerator coroutine(): Allows for asynchronous scripting. Use this to run tasks over time, often with WaitForSeconds."
