"""What's the issue of adding too many regressor in an OLS when trying to estimate a causal effect ?","""

""Adding too many regressors in an OLS regression when trying to estimate a causal effect can lead to several issues:

1. Multicollinearity: Including too many correlated variables can inflate standard errors, reducing statistical power and making it difficult to determine the significance of individual coefficients.

2.isode Biasedness: If some regressors are correlated with the error term, they can introduce bias into the estimated coefficients, even when the model is correctly specified.

3. Overfitting: Including more than necessary variables can lead to a model that fits the training data well but poorly generalizes to new data, especially if panic rootESS seems too large.

