 dwóch pasz CIMosa:

To write a good research proposal, start by clearly defining your research question or problem. This should be concise and well-stated, typically around 2-3 sentences in length. Your proposal should outline your research objectives, highlighting the significance and可行度 of your work.

Next, you'll want to document your knowledge of related literature and – If applicable – explain how your research contributes to or differing from existing studies. This helps establish the novelty and importance of your work.

