"""will very green pineapples ripen?"," some people stated that it can not be possible and will will not ripen and some stated that is possible to ripen""

Yes, it is possible for deep green pineapples to ripen. While most pineapples we see in stores are yellow, green pineapples are actually the early stage of ripe pineapples.

The ripening process of a pineapple begins with green coloration that gradually turns to yellow. As the pineapple ripens, its color changes from deep green to bright yellow. The darker green indicates that the pineapple is still in the early stages of its ripening process.

It's important to note that the ripeness of a pineapple isn't solely determined by its color. Other factors like the texture of the skin, the weight, and the smell can also indicate when a pineapple is ready to eat.

If you have a deep green pineapple at home, the best thing you can do is monitor it closely. As it ripens, it will gradually turn yellow. However, if it doesn't develop that characteristic yellow color within a week or so after purchase, then it may not ripen further.

For more information on how to tell if a pineapple is ripe, you can refer to this removed context important for understanding."
