As for becoming a pro surfer, it's a long and challenging journey. On average, it can take anywhere from 5 to 10 years of consistent practice to reach professional levels. This journey involves:

1. Mastering the basics
2. Improving your skill and technique
3. Competing at local and regional levels
4. Building a professional network
5. Developing your own style and identity
