"""I am playing tic tac toe with a friend.\\nHe started placing a circle in the center. I put a cross in the upper left corner. He then played a circle in the top center position.\\nWhere should I play next?"," In the bottom center for a tie? Or in the lower right to win? Or should I block him by putting a cross in the upper right corner?""

The optimal move in this tic-tac-toe game is to play in the upper right corner. This move allows you to create a winning diagonal from the top center to the lower right, securing your victory. 

By placing your cross in the upper right, youerald the opponent's attempts to draw a tie (if they were to play in the bottom center) and simultaneously cut off one of their potential winning diagonals (e.g., lower left to upper right).

This strategy not only guarantees your win but also neutralizes the opponent's next best move, making it the most effective choice in this particular tic-tac-toe scenario."
